// Types the standard library declares in Jadpo (docs/compiler-runtime.md
// §2.1). The representation types (`Bool`, `Int`, `Decimal`, `Text`,
// `Bytes`, `Uuid`), the validated text types (`Email`, `Url`, `IpAddress`),
// the time types and `Unit` are built into the checker, because no Jadpo
// declaration can say what they are made of. `Rounding`, `TextFormat` and
// `UuidVersion` are declared once in `jadpo-std`, beside the Rust code that
// interprets them, and the checker reads them from there.

/// How a failure reaches a client and how background work treats it
/// (area 4). An application declares only `invalid_value`, `not_found`,
/// `not_permitted`, `conflict`, `rejected`, `rate_limited` and
/// `unavailable`; the runtime raises the rest (question 3).
public type FailureKind = Enum {
    invalid_request
    invalid_value
    unauthenticated
    not_permitted
    not_visible
    not_found
    conflict
    precondition_failed
    rejected
    rate_limited
    unavailable
    timed_out
    outcome_unknown
    misconfigured
    internal_fault
}
